{"result":"{
  "id": "18827",
  "key": "SFCC-463",
  "summary": "Price Display Consistency — PWA Rendering Across All Surfaces",
  "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/issue/18827",
  "description": "**As a** Shopper, \n**I want** to see prices displayed consistently in my local currency across every surface of the site, \n**so that** I always see the correct price regardless of where I am browsing.\n\nThe PWA must render the correct price consistently across: PLP, PDP, cart, wishlist, recommended product tiles, order history, recently viewed and checkout. The price source is either the SFCC pricebook for that storefront and currency, or — where no SFCC pricebook exists for the shopper's currency — the Global-e converted price derived from the base pricebook.\n\nThis is a PWA Kit frontend story. Currency display formatting rules (symbol, decimal places, separators) are configured in BM per [SFCC-46](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-46). \nCountry-to-currency mapping is configured per [SFCC-44](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-44). This story ensures the PWA applies those rules consistently across all surfaces.\n\n\n\nReference Image (Figma is leading)\n\n![\"image-20260901-052147.png\"](image-20260901-052147.png)\n\n![\"image-20260901-052244.png\"](image-20260901-052244.png)",
